        "id": 9260,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-13T04:45:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So, I've had my RC/IR box set for about a month now, and I've noticed a very pronounced curvature developing in all of the new cards.&nbsp; It makes little actual difference, since new and old decks don't mix, but it bugs me.&nbsp; Has anyone else had this problem, and is there a terribly easy fix for it?&nbsp; I know if I put in a little elbow grease bending the cards back, or pressed them flat under heavy books over a series of weeks, it would correct the problem, but I'm hoping for a less labor-intensive solution.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:59.591Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
